feat(oracle): read-access / abuse-protection layer for providers oracle

Rename contracts/oracles/pyth/ -> providers/ (shared base for Pyth and
Chainlink), add a ChainlinkOracle skeleton, and add an abuse-protection
read layer to the providers OracleBase:

- IPoolFactory interface (isPool, inSwap) consumed by the oracle.
- Per-feed paid pool registration (register, payable) validated via an
  approved pool factory; ADMIN-managed approved-factory set; per-pool
  blacklist (deny-list) with paid redemption; external-integrator
  whitelist with its own read path; settable registrationFee.
- Monetized on-chain read price(feedId, factory): approved factory +
  inSwap proof + registeredPool + blacklist, emits PriceRead; plus
  integratorPrice for whitelisted integrators. View reads stay open,
  blacklist-gated on msg.sender.
- oracleData made internal and Extsload dropped from the providers
  OracleBase so the blacklist read-gate has no raw storage-slot bypass.
- Move EthWithdrawn/withdrawEth into the shared base/interface.
- Tests (OracleBaseAbuseProtection.t.sol, MockPoolFactory) + EN/RU
  integration docs; exclude debug.t.sol from forge test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
